Step 1 – Create Cognito User Pool
1. Open AWS Console → Amazon Cognito.
2. Select User pools → Create user pool.
3. Select application type: Traditional web application or the closest browser-based application option.
4. Application name: day2-auth-app.
5. Select Username as the sign-in identifier.
6. Authentication: Username and password.
7. Do not enable MFA.
8. Create the User Pool.
Step 2 – Create App Client
In the User Pool:
1. Open App clients.
2. Create an app client named day2-auth-web-client.
3. Do not generate a client secret.
4. Enable ALLOW_USER_PASSWORD_AUTH and ALLOW_REFRESH_TOKEN_AUTH if configuring the authentication flows manually.
5. Save.
Step 3 – Create demo user
Under User Pool → Users:

Create:
Field	Value
Username	student1
Password	Student@123

Set the password as permanent if Cognito asks you to choose between temporary and permanent.
Step 4 – Connect your application
We will modify only login.html to authenticate directly against Cognito using the Amplify JavaScript library.

The application will use:
- User Pool ID
- App Client ID
- AWS Region: ap-south-1
After successful login, redirect to Dashboard.html. Otherwise, redirect to Login_failure.html.
Step 5 – Upload updated frontend
Replace the existing login.html in S3 and invalidate the CloudFront cache.
